From: niu-git
Subject: [PATCH] run-command: fail cleanly when no POSIX shell is on PATH

Justification (see patches/README.md): niu-git deliberately ships no POSIX
interpreter (wpm/niugit.json: "hooks run via sh found on PATH"). Git for
Windows never runs this code with a missing shell, because its bundled
sh.exe is always first on PATH; niu-git exercises it and paid the bill.

Upstream, git_shell_path()'s windows branch hands the NULL that
locate_in_PATH("sh") returns when no shell is reachable straight into
convert_slashes(), and the inline loop in compat/mingw.h dereferences
it: every use_shell command - "!"-aliases above all - dies with an
access violation (exit 0xC0000005) and no output. unixwin/niu-git#14.

Guard the NULL, and make prepare_shell_cmd(), the one place a missing
shell is fatal, die() with a message that names the command that
needed a shell and what was missed, instead of crashing:

    fatal: cannot run 'echo hi': no shell found on PATH

POSIX (non-native) builds are untouched: there git_shell_path() returns
the build-time SHELL_PATH and never NULL. "git var GIT_SHELL_PATH" on a
shellless install now exits 1 with no output (var.c already treats a
NULL read as unset) instead of taking the process down.

---
--- a/run-command.c
+++ b/run-command.c
@@ -279,8 +279,16 @@ char *git_shell_path(void)
 #ifndef GIT_WINDOWS_NATIVE
 	return xstrdup(SHELL_PATH);
 #else
+	/*
+	 * niu-git bases shell-script execution on the sh found on PATH and
+	 * ships no interpreter of its own; locate_in_PATH() then returns
+	 * NULL. Handing that NULL to convert_slashes() dereferenced it and
+	 * killed the process with an access violation, so guard it: callers
+	 * treat a NULL return as "there is no shell" and fail cleanly.
+	 */
 	char *p = locate_in_PATH("sh");
-	convert_slashes(p);
+	if (p)
+		convert_slashes(p);
 	return p;
 #endif
 }
@@ -291,7 +299,11 @@ static const char **prepare_shell_cmd(struct strvec *out, const char **argv)
 		BUG("shell command is empty");
 
 	if (strcspn(argv[0], "|&;<>()$`\\\"' \t\n*?[#~=%") != strlen(argv[0])) {
-		strvec_push_nodup(out, git_shell_path());
+		char *shell = git_shell_path();
+
+		if (!shell)
+			die(_("cannot run '%s': no shell found on PATH"), argv[0]);
+		strvec_push_nodup(out, shell);
 		strvec_push(out, "-c");
 
 		/*
